<%#
  The plugin's settings screen (WP5).

  One setting so far: how much a single row or column action on a workflow
  matrix may change before it asks. Rendered by Redmine inside its own
  box.tabular.settings, so the markup is core's -- a label, a field and an
  em.info -- and the plugin adds no styling of its own.

  The field shows the number that is actually in force, not an empty box, so an
  administrator who saves this page without touching it keeps what was there.
%>
<p>
  <label for="settings_bulk_confirm_threshold">
    <%= l(:label_project_workflow_bulk_confirm_threshold) %>
  </label>
  <%= text_field_tag 'settings[bulk_confirm_threshold]',
                     settings['bulk_confirm_threshold'].presence ||
                       RedmineProjectWorkflows::BulkActionsHelper::DEFAULT_BULK_CONFIRM_THRESHOLD,
                     id: 'settings_bulk_confirm_threshold', size: 6 %>
  <em class="info"><%= l(:text_project_workflow_bulk_confirm_threshold) %></em>
</p>
